WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.100
Speaker 1: Donald Trump's tax returns are going&nbsp;
public on Friday. It's finally happening. We&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:09.780
already know much of what is in those tax returns,&nbsp;
thanks to the report issued by the January&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:14.820
six committee. But we're getting them. The tax&nbsp;
returns are going to be released Friday and it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:19.560
going to be wild. NBC News reporting Trump tax&nbsp;
returns to be released to the public on Friday.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:26.160
The Ways and Means Committee voted last week to&nbsp;
make six years of Trump's tax returns public.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:32.280
This was a party line vote. Initially, the&nbsp;
plan was to release the documents as early&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:37.680
as last Wednesday. The disclosure was delayed&nbsp;
due to having to redact personal information&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:43.620
like Social Security numbers. The assortment&nbsp;
of six years of Trump's personal tax returns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:48.420
and some of his business returns are expected to&nbsp;
be placed into the Congressional Record Friday.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:54.120
The clock is ticking for the committee, which&nbsp;
will turn over control to Republicans when the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.120 --> 00:01:01.440
new Congress is sworn in next week. Another report&nbsp;
from Reuters. Former Republican President Donald&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:07.740
Trump's redacted tax returns will be made public&nbsp;
on Friday. The documents to be released Friday are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:14.400
expected to include a Trump's tax returns between&nbsp;
2015 and 2021, the years he ran for and served as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:21.000
president. A spokesperson for Trump declined&nbsp;
to comment. Trump was the first presidential&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:27.060
candidate in decades not to release his tax&nbsp;
returns during either of his campaigns for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:33.840
president. So beyond the Trump aspects of this,&nbsp;
what are we going to learn from the Trump aspects?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:40.020
Okay, we've gone over it so many times. He's not&nbsp;
as rich as he claims to be. He has sketchy debts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:47.580
that raise questions about being compromised in&nbsp;
national security. He uses this. Some would call&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:52.560
it fraudulent technique of inflating the value&nbsp;
of assets when he wants to use the asset as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:57.540
collateral for a loan, but diminishing the value&nbsp;
of an asset when it's for the purposes of figuring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.540 --> 00:02:03.360
out how much tax he's going to owe on that asset.&nbsp;
There's the Trump aspect to it. We already learned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:07.440
most of those things are true from the summary&nbsp;
the House released, and we will get, I believe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:12.780
beyond a shadow of a doubt, confirmation&nbsp;
from the tax returns themselves. Beyond that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:19.740
there are banks that will maybe end up under&nbsp;
pressure after these tax returns are released&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:24.960
to know from people wanting to know from those&nbsp;
banks, why did you keep loaning this guy money&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:32.400
when his finances were clearly bad? How did&nbsp;
you accept this valuation for a building&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:36.660
that was serving as collateral when it's so&nbsp;
clearly was not the value of the building?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:41.280
So I believe there's going to be attention on&nbsp;
banks and whether the banks were sort of like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:48.060
look the other way or whether the banks were&nbsp;
complicit in what some would call a fraud.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:56.460
We are also going to see potentially the&nbsp;
argument made that, you know, something is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.460 --> 00:03:01.620
partizan and biased here because there has never&nbsp;
been this much attention about any president's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:06.660
tax returns. The right is going to say, you&nbsp;
know, this is all a politically trumped up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:10.440
witch hunt. Way to go after Donald Trump, because&nbsp;
you've never seen so many people waiting for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:17.880
tax returns of another president. Well, no other&nbsp;
president. Refused to release their tax returns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:24.780
and then worked for six years to prevent their&nbsp;
release. That's why there is a spotlight on this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:29.940
and they will claim. The problem is that&nbsp;
people are eager to see the tax returns. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:34.620
the reason we're even in this situation is&nbsp;
because Trump did something nobody else has done,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:39.660
which is to say, I'm just not going to release&nbsp;
them now. He did say, I will release them once.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:44.460
They're no longer being audited, but they weren't&nbsp;
being audited. And you all know the lies. But the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:51.360
point here is what's unique isn't that the tax&nbsp;
returns are coming out. It's that they had to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:56.640
come out via this means because Trump refused to&nbsp;
otherwise provide them. So don't fall for that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.640 --> 00:04:01.800
when we certainly hear from Republicans, you&nbsp;
know, this is political partizanship because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:07.260
Democrats are excited about the tax returns. Now&nbsp;
it's Trump who did the thing nobody else has done.

